2026-07-08 18:05:19    FORMULA : To determine which technicians are carrying the heaviest workload, I will first identify all "Open" work orders across both the BDM and PPM modules. For BDM, I will group the open work orders by the assigned "AnalysisTechName" and "ExecutionTechName" separately. For PPM, I will group open work orders by "PMTechName". I will ensure to exclude any blank or null technician assignments from the counts, as these do not represent a technician's workload.
2026-07-08 18:05:19    CALL : group_by_and_count | module=bdm | filter_field=WoStatus | group_field=AnalysisTechName | filter_value=Open
2026-07-08 18:05:19    RESULT : total = 839  |  top → (unassigned) = 539,  Technician = 218,  Employee18 (capital cateringTech) = 48,  Janitor = 12,  eashaktech = 4
2026-07-08 18:05:19    FORMULA : My approach will be to identify the workload for technicians from both the breakdown maintenance (bdm) and planned preventive maintenance (ppm) modules. For the bdm module, I will count open work orders assigned to technicians in both `AnalysisTechName` and `ExecutionTechName` fields. For the ppm module, I will count open work orders assigned to technicians in the `PMTechName` field. I will then combine and sum these counts to determine the total workload per technician, and identify the top technicians with the heaviest workload.
2026-07-08 18:05:19    CALL : group_by_and_count | module=bdm | group_field=ExecutionTechName | filter_field=WoStatus | filter_value=Open
